{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010152-can-supernal-magic-create-substances-of-a-kind-with-a-specific-symbolic-attribute","id":1010152,"title":"Can Supernal Magic create substances of a kind with a specific symbolic attribute?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-30T04:56:50-08:00","id":1010152,"title":"Can Supernal Magic create substances of a kind with a specific symbolic attribute?","content":"I think the topic title probably needs a bit of explanation. The question is whether products of Supernal magic can be given specific attributes within the Imago that is not inherent to the product being created, but is a possible symbolic attribute of a thing anyway?<br /> <br /> A piece of iron created through Matter is obviously a piece of iron, but can I make it a piece of iron that acts symbolically as if it was mined in the Swedish mountains? What about water that is symbolically identical to the clear water from a Tyrolean mountain spring? Can a Matter mage create a knife that acts as if it had been the bloody murder weapon of a serial killer? Can a Life mage create a plant that acts as if it had been manured by the blood of the innocently convicted?<br /> <br /> Such things can matter when dealing with the Bans and Banes of various Ephemeral Entities and some Horrors.<br /> <br /> I remember the teaser about Perfected materials mentioning that one of the neat advantages they have is that they circumvent such specific restrictions, but can a mage create more specific variations of things without resorting to Perfected materials?<br /> <br /> An interesting follow-up question might be whether such creations potentially attract Spirits and similar entities drawn to these specific attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:31:01-08:00","id":1010159,"title":"","content":"I would say no, and if you have Prime it hardly matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:07:56-08:00","id":1010166,"title":"","content":"Check-out Prime 3 Ephemeral Enhancement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:18:17-08:00","id":1010171,"title":"","content":"And if you don't have Prime use Space to borrow or create the sympathetic connection the object needs. Bascially everything you discribe is a sympathetic connection to a place or person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:21:21-08:00","id":1010173,"title":"","content":"I'd say those are Making spells, with a Space (&quot;mined in the Swedish mountains&quot;, &quot;identical to the clear water from a Tyrolean mountain spring&quot;) or Fate (&quot;the bloody murder weapon of a serial killer&quot;, &quot;manured by the blood of the innocently convicted&quot;) component. So, not easy, but definitely possible (without Prime, to boot).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:00:13-08:00","id":1010187,"title":"","content":"re Prime: While I am thankful for the replies, I am aware of Ephemeral Enchantment. That, however, was not my question. I only mentioned the Bans and Banes to give an example of when such questions might matter. Ephemeral Enchantment does not actually answer the question in any way, it just shows a different way to get a similar result. Quite apart from the fact that not every Mage is going to have access to Prime 3. That being said, I could definitely imagine other Prime spells investing the thing with enough Truth of that particular kind.<br /> <br /> re: Space: Hmmm... I could potentially see that for those that require a specific place, but not sure for those requiring a different circumstance. What Practice would you say that is? Ruling, like Borrow Threads?<br /> <br /> re: Fate: Making of Fate sounds accurate, yes, but can a Fate be retroactively changed without the Imperial Practices? Otherwise I would imagine the Making of Fate would just make it so that the thing in question <i>will become </i>that which the Mage wants (the knife gets picked up by a serial killer, for instance).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: To give an example of when this might matter aside from Bans and Banes, consider Quintessence. Can a Mage create Quintessence without any arduous search by just making something that is reasonably close to the sought-after Quintessence into Quintessence by changing that particular attribute of the thing with a non-Imperial spell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 11-30-2016, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:11:35-08:00","id":1010192,"title":"","content":"Mages don't need Quintessence and considering its unique importance to archmasters I'd say no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:25:15-08:00","id":1010194,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that trick would work for most things but quintessence just feels like it would be pickier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:36:26-08:00","id":1010197,"title":"","content":"Unless the Mage is a master of Matter and Time, whereupon they can create an object with a known history, Mages shouldn't really be able to create objects of specific provenance.<br /> <br /> That said, if they can find the source of the object's specialness, maybe they can recreate that? A vengeance spirit might suffer a Bane of a murder weapon that was used to kill an innocent, because the resonance of that weapon is toxic to it. By producing that same resonance on another weapon, a Mage may make it also a bane.<br /> <br /> Quintessences absolutely should not be able to be made with a spell... Unless the Quintessence is aboit the product specifically about that spell. Then it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:27:23-08:00","id":1010210,"title":"","content":"Every property of an object you discribed so far is in my opinion under the purview of Space. If a knife belonged to a murderer it has a sympathetic connection to that said murderer. In my opinion you cannot recreate this with Fate.<br /> It get's more difficult if the property gets more obscure, like &quot;was created under a full moon in a cold night&quot;. I am unsure if such a property could be given to an object at all, probably only with Time or Prime 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010152-can-supernal-magic-create-substances-of-a-kind-with-a-specific-symbolic-attribute?p=1010187#post1010187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">re: Space: Hmmm... I could potentially see that for those that require a specific place, but not sure for those requiring a different circumstance. What Practice would you say that is? Ruling, like Borrow Threads?</div> </div> </div> </div>As said above Space is not about places, but about connection. You can either &quot;steal&quot; this connection from another subject which has the desired properties with ruling (Borrow Threads), attach a new connection to the object and the desired subject with perfecting (Web-Weaver) or create an outright new connection to anything fitting with making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:46:39-08:00","id":1010217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010152-can-supernal-magic-create-substances-of-a-kind-with-a-specific-symbolic-attribute?p=1010210#post1010210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every property of an object you discribed so far is in my opinion under the purview of Space. If a knife belonged to a murderer it has a sympathetic connection to that said murderer. In my opinion you cannot recreate this with Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sympathetic connection will erode over time until it has disappeared completely, but as far as I know bans and banes have no expiration date. It's not the sympathetic connection to the murderer that gives the knife the &quot;murder weapon&quot; quality. That quality is inherent in the knife since the moment it was used in a murder independently of its sympathetic connections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:53:53-08:00","id":1010218,"title":"","content":"Certain sympathetic connections may not erode, ever, by simple dint of their defining nature. For example, a person always has Strong sympathy to their biological parents. There's also conceptual connections to consider: That the knife may always have a connection to murder as a concept, and always has temporal sympathy to the murder itself until and unless it's melted down and reduced to slag.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what quality it is that makes something a Bane or Ban subject - it is a Mystery - but sympathy can't be flatly ruled out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:30:29-08:00","id":1010303,"title":"","content":"I would lean towards no. Different game and magic system, but I like the setting assumption in Unknown Armies that you can't use magic to directly get around the restrictions of other magic. IMO, giving mages an incentive to go out and interact with the Fallen World in pursuit of their Obsessions (IE, getting their hands on an actual murder weapon) is a better outcome than letting them skip that step with a quick instant spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T23:48:35-08:00","id":1010537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1010152-can-supernal-magic-create-substances-of-a-kind-with-a-specific-symbolic-attribute?p=1010303#post1010303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would lean towards no. Different game and magic system, but I like the setting assumption in Unknown Armies that you can't use magic to directly get around the restrictions of other magic. IMO, giving mages an incentive to go out and interact with the Fallen World in pursuit of their Obsessions (IE, getting their hands on an actual murder weapon) is a better outcome than letting them skip that step with a quick instant spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree, but so far there was nothing discussed short of at least one Arcanum at 5 dots to &quot;simply&quot; give an object such kind of property, so I don't think it is done with a quick instant spell anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T00:19:46-08:00","id":1010543,"title":"","content":"I would probably allow borrowing &quot;qualities&quot; from one item to another using 3rd dot of Matter, transforming one into another with 4th, and flat out creating new ones at 5th. The trick is to be able to target &quot;the quality&quot; itself, which would probably need some kind of support magic, which could come from Fate, Prime or something else depending on your needs. And by support Magic I don't mean &quot;add Fate 1 to the spell&quot;, but &quot;run a Fate spell in the background&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}